    /// <remarks>
    ///   <para>owl:Class</para>
    ///   <para>A symbolic is recognized as reference unit also if it is not part of a quantity (e.g. as in the sentence "the Bq is the reference unit of Becquerel").
    /// For this reason we can't declare the axiom:
    /// MetrologicalReference SubClassOf: inverse(hasMetrologicalReference) some Quantity
    /// because there exist reference units without being part of a quantity.
    /// This is peculiar to EMMO, where quantities as syntatic entities (explicit quantities) are distinct with quantities as semantic entities (properties).</para>
    ///   <para>A reference can be a measurement unit, a measurement procedure, a reference material, or a combination of such (VIM3 1.1 NOTE 2).</para>
