    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    ///   <para>owl:Class</para>
    ///   <para>The class constrast individuals standing for entities that can stimulate a perception (e.g. a retina impression) to a human being and that are categorized accordingly to human perception mechanisms.</para>
    ///   <para>This class is the most general superclass for the categorization of contrasts that are perceivable through a specific human-related perception mechanism. This perspective is based on human characterization of perceptions.
    /// A 'Perceptual' can stand for another object in an EMMO described semiotic process (acting as sign or as object), just like a word on a paper (the perceptual object) may refer semiotically to another object. However, a perceptual is not necessarily a 'Sign' (e.g. a line sketched on a blackboard is a recognizable 'Perceptual' but it may stand for nothing).
    /// A 'Perceptual' becomes a semiotic object, when it is part of a 'Semiotic' process described by the ontologist within the EMMO, and it's done always specifying for which interpreter this relation occurs.</para>
    /// labels<para>Perceptual</para></remarks>
    /// <seealso href="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_649bf97b_4397_4005_90d9_219755d92e34">https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_649bf97b_4397_4005_90d9_219755d92e34</seealso>
