    ///   <para>owl:Class</para>
    ///   <para>The disjoint union of Causal Path and CausalSystem classes.</para>
    ///   <para>A causal structure expresses itself in time and space thanks to the underlying causality relations between its constituent quantum entities. It must at least provide two temporal parts. The unity criterion beyond the definition of a causal structure (the most general concept of structure) is the existence of an undirected causal path between each of its parts.</para>
