    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    ///   <para>owl:Class</para>
    ///   <para>A state that is a collection of sufficiently large number of other parts such that:
    /// - it is the bearer of qualities that can exists only by the fact that it is a sum of parts
    /// - the smallest partition dV of the state volume in which we are interested in, contains enough parts to be statistically consistent: n [#/m3] x dV [m3] &gt;&gt; 1</para>
    ///   <para>A continuum is made of a sufficient number of parts that it continues to exists as continuum individual even after the loss of one of them i.e. a continuum is a redundant.</para>
