    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    ///   <para>owl:Class</para>
    ///   <para>A composite physical object is made of bonded objects (i.e. characterised by their quantum states using a Schrodinger equation approach) that are connected together by elementary particles travelling between them. These elemenentary particles are real particles, describing the existance of a classical field (e.g. Coulomb potential between charged particles).</para>
    ///   <para>The class of physical objects possessing a structure that is larger than a single composite particle, for which its bosonic or fermionic nature is undetermined.</para>
    /// labels<para>CompositePhysicalObject</para></remarks>
    /// <seealso href="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_57d977ab_0036_4779_b59a_e47620afdb9c">https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_57d977ab_0036_4779_b59a_e47620afdb9c</seealso>
